/* DARK MESSAGE BOXES (FT only, Nils 2026-07-30). Info_Box / Stop_Box / YesNo_Box end up in the
   Win32 MessageBox API, which Windows draws itself - no colour hook, no dark mode - so a message box
   in the theme has to be a dialog of its own. Since 2026-09-29 that is the RDCFlexTron library's
   (FTMessageBox.pkg, shown in FTMessageBox.dg): FTInfoBox / FTStopBox / FTYesNoBox as drop-in
   equivalents (same call shapes, same MBR_Yes/MBR_No return, same Num_Arguments handling), and
   FTHtmlMessage for a formatted body with verb buttons. DFRefactor's own RefactorInfoBox /
   RefactorStopBox / RefactorYesNoBox, in MessageBoxFT.dg, did this until then.

   #REPLACE WAS THE PLAN AND IT DOES NOT WORK - measured, not assumed. The idea was three
   #REPLACE lines here redirecting all 195 call sites without editing any file. Three probes
   settled it: pointing the replacement at a nonexistent procedure compiled clean (DataFlex
   tolerates unknown message names in Send), and so did pointing it at the KEYWORD End_Procedure -
   including for a "Get FTYesNoBox ... to iRetval" later in THIS very file, so no ordering doubt.
   #REPLACE substitutes in command, type and expression positions (which is how the runtime uses
   it for CP_UTF8, OLE_Handle and the rest) but NOT in the message-name slot after Send / Get.
   Since these three are only ever reached that way, the whole approach is dead.

   So the conversion is per-call-site, and only in FT-ONLY files - 68 of them across 17 files,
   which is every message box on the FlexTron-specific surface. The other ~127 live in engine and
   funclib code SHARED with the two light builds, where a swap would darken their boxes too; those
   keep the system box until each gets an FT variant for other reasons. */
Use FTMessageBox.pkg            // FTInfoBox / FTStopBox / FTYesNoBox / FTHtmlMessage (RDCFlexTron)
Use FTRefactorMessageBox.pkg    // ghoBrowsePackages + ShowPicker - declared early

Use cWorkspaceMenuItem.pkg
Use cEncodingHelpers.pkg
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg     // ElemHtml / ChipHtml / BarButtonHtml - global, so every
                             // dialog can build a chip whatever the include order.

// clDarkViewBg / clDarkWebBg moved to RefactorConstants.h.pkg (Used at the top of this file), so the
// ~28 FT files that reference them no longer depend on being Used below this point.

// FT: last Modernize/analyze outcome, cached so the dashboard's "Last analyze" tile can show it on return.
// ModAnalyzerFT.dg writes these when the analyze summary is built; DashboardFT.vw reads them in
// RefreshAnalyze. Kept as FT-only globals - no change to the shared cRefactorApplication.
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastAnalyzeAuto      // auto-fixable rows
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastAnalyzeSuggest   // rows to review
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastAnalyzeWarn      // compiler warning messages
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastAnalyzeErr       // compiler error messages
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastAnalyzeDone      // 0 = not analyzed for the current workspace, 1 = have a result
Global_Variable String  ghsLastAnalyzeDate      // ISO yyyy-mm-dd of the cached counts above ("" = none); shown as "last run <date>"
Global_Variable String  ghsLastAnalyzeProgram   // the program (.src) the cached counts are for - labels the Modernize tile so a many-program workspace is not ambiguous ("" = unknown/old snapshot)
Global_Variable String  ghsLastAnalyzeWS        // the .sws path the cached counts/date describe; RefreshAnalyze re-seeds from the registry snapshot when this <> psSWSFile (robust to any workspace-load path)

// FT: the CURRENT saved LastPlan file's profile - drives the SHARED "View/Run last plan" link + the guided
// "Run Plan" button, which BOTH a compile+analyze cycle AND a Deep Scan can produce (the plan JSON is shared,
// latest writer wins). Set at every plan write (ModAnalyzerFT.dg LoadData) and restored from the file header on
// workspace load (DashboardFT.RestoreAnalyzeSnapshot). Deliberately SEPARATE from ghiLastAnalyze* above (which
// stay the COMPILE stat readout / burn-down cue) so a Deep Scan plan resumes like an analyze plan without ever
// polluting the compile counts. "" / 0 => no resumable plan for this workspace.
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastPlanAuto         // auto-fix rows in the saved LastPlan (either source)
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastPlanSuggest      // review rows in the saved LastPlan (either source)
Global_Variable Integer ghiLastPlanIsDeepScan   // 1 = the saved LastPlan was written by a Deep Scan (labels the foot); 0 = compile+analyze
Global_Variable String  ghsLastPlanDate         // ISO yyyy-mm-dd of the saved LastPlan ("" = none)
Global_Variable Handle  ghoTabWorkspace         // FT EXPERIMENT: CodeJock MDI tab-workspace (cCJTabWorkspace) handle, captured in oCJCommandBarSystem.OnCreateTabbedWorkspace; the docked OutputDockFT re-asserts ComEnableGroups on it to try to revive drag-to-split view grouping after a tool panel docks

// FT: declared HERE (before the views are Used) so ModAnalyzerFT.dg can Broadcast it to oDashboard_vw when
// an analyze finishes - the dashboard view may not re-activate after the (docked) analyze, so its Activating
// hook alone is unreliable. The procedure is DEFINED in DashboardFT.vw; the Broadcast no-ops on any view
// that does not handle it.
Register_Procedure RefreshAnalyze
Register_Procedure SourceReverted
Register_Procedure AnalysisCleared    // broadcast by the Test Compile bar's Clear (TestCompileFT.dg)

// FT: declared HERE (before the views are Used) so the Select Folders / Select Functions views can Broadcast
// it to oDashboard_vw whenever the user changes the selection (a tick, or Select All/None/Invert). In the
// side-by-side Split View the dashboard stays visible beside those grids, so it never re-Activates and its
// "Selected" tile would otherwise go stale. The procedure is DEFINED in DashboardFT.vw, where it just arms
// the existing coalescing refresh timer; the Broadcast no-ops on any view that does not handle it.
Register_Procedure RequestTileRefresh

/* ORPHANED BY THE 2026-08-10 DASHBOARD SWAP - registered here so the Broadcasts still COMPILE.

   TestCompileFT.dg broadcasts RunDeepScan (the bar's own scan chip) and RunDeepScanVerify (the
   post-plan automatic verify re-scan). Both workers lived on the old split cockpit board, which is
   no longer in the build, and the guided board that replaced it does not answer either message -
   it drives its scans through ghoDeepScanDriver from its own Check flow instead.

   Without these two registrations the .src does not compile at all (4306 on the Broadcast). WITH
   them it compiles and the two broadcasts reach nobody: the Test Compile bar's Deep Scan chip and
   the auto verify re-scan are INERT until the guided board answers them. Deliberate and visible
   rather than silent - see the swap's commit message for the full orphan list. */
Register_Procedure RunDeepScan
Register_Procedure RunDeepScanVerify

// Not sure why we need this, but it somehow is linked to the "OnIdle events"
Procedure Exit_Application for cDesktop
    // Arm pbAppExiting BEFORE Exit_System_Confirmation/Abort. A committed exit TERMINATES inside the
    // Abort below, so anything after it never runs on a real exit - which is exactly why this flag
    // stayed False during teardown and the Modernize dock's restore-on-return re-showed against
    // half-destroyed CodeJock COM objects -> error 4399 (pvComObject NULL in ComEnableGroups). It
    // only bites when exiting from a NON-editor view with the Modernize pane open: the CJ MDI
    // activates the editor view as it tears the views down, and that view's Activate handler
    // re-shows the dock unless this flag is already set (ShowTestCompileDockOnly checks it). Set it
    // up front so the guard is armed no matter which branch runs. One-way latch by design (see
    // pbAppExiting in cRefactorApplication.pkg) - never reset; a cancelled exit merely leaves the
    // dock not auto-restoring until the next launch. (Nils 2026-07-06.)
    Set pbAppExiting of ghoApplication to True
    Send SuspendGUI of Desktop True
    If (Exit_System_Confirmation(Self)) ;
        Abort
End_Procedure

