Use cFolderSelDtlDataDictionary.dd
    Procedure StartRefactoreCode
        Handle hoEditor hoDD hoStatusBar hoTC
        tRefactorFiles RefactorFiles
        String sFileFilter
        Integer iRetval
        Boolean bGuidedRun bWsMode

        Move False to Err
        // CollectFileData scans the selected folders and can take a while before the engine's Yes/No question
        // appears - show the wait cursor + a status-bar note so the click feels responsive (both reset before
        // the question pops). PumpMsgQueue flushes the paint so the text shows before the synchronous scan.
        Send Cursor_Wait of Cursor_Control
        Get Statusbar_Id of (phoMainPanel(ghoApplication)) to hoStatusBar
        Set StatusText of hoStatusBar to "Collecting data for manual refactoring..."
        Send PumpMsgQueue of Desktop
        Get Create (RefClass(cFolderSelDtlDataDictionary)) to hoDD
        Get CollectFileData of ghoApplication hoDD to RefactorFiles
        Send Destroy of hoDD
        Send Cursor_Ready of Cursor_Control
        Set StatusText of hoStatusBar to ""
        Get phoEditor of ghoApplication to hoEditor
        If (Err = True) Begin
            Procedure_Return
        End

        // Start the Engine!
        Set peRunOrigin of ghoEngine to eRunManual
        Send StartEngine of ghoEngine RefactorFiles hoEditor
        // MANUAL-RUN VERIFY HANDOFF (Nils 2026-07-16): a manual pass (Tidy Up, workspace or single
        // file) that CHANGED files has a natural next step - compile and check nothing was mangled.
        // The scan loop auto re-scans (cheap, scope already confirmed); a compile needs a PROGRAM
        // pick, so ASK, and on Yes just OPEN the Test Compile dock - the user picks the program in
        // its combo and presses Compile, nothing auto-starts (Nils's chosen shape).
        // SysFile.iCountNumberOfChangedFiles is zeroed per run (InitializeEngine -> ResetSysFile)
        // and counts THIS run's changed files. A READ-ONLY run still tallies would-be changes, so
        // it is excluded - nothing was written, nothing to verify. Plan/scan-origin runs enter via
        // StartAutoSelect, never here, so this cannot double up with the compile loop's post-run
        // relight or the scan loop's auto verify re-scan. A /bm batch run force-exits inside
        // StartEngine and never reaches this point.
        /* IF THE GUIDED TRAIL SENT THE USER HERE, SEND THEM BACK (Nils 2026-07-29) - and OUTSIDE the
           changed-files gate, which is what stranded him. A Tidy Up over 1,796 files that changed
           NOTHING skipped this block entirely, so the trail never came back and its stepper never
           learned the stage had run: "after the tidy up was done, the (WIP) page was not activated."
           Whether a run found anything is a fact about the run; being returned to the flow you were
           following is not conditional on it.

           A run that CHANGED files has something to verify, so it offers Check. One that changed
           nothing has nothing to verify and just goes back. Either way the stage is recorded, so the
           stepper can mark step 4. The flag is ONE-SHOT, so a pass the user starts on their own still
           gets the Test Compile handoff below, which is right for it. */
        Get pbGuidedTidyUpRun of ghoApplication to bGuidedRun
        If (bGuidedRun = True) Begin
            Set pbGuidedTidyUpRun of ghoApplication to False
            // Stamped BEFORE the offer below, and the dirty half is independent of the ANSWER:
            // whether the run left unverified changes is a fact about the run, not about what the
            // user chose to do next. Persisted per workspace, so the trail's Tidy Up stage and its
            // Ready badge survive a restart (see WriteTidyUpStamp).
            Send WriteTidyUpStamp of ghoApplication (SysFile.iCountNumberOfChangedFiles > 0 and SysFile.bReadOnly = False)
            If (SysFile.iCountNumberOfChangedFiles > 0 and SysFile.bReadOnly = False) Begin
                Get FTYesNoBox ("The run changed" * String(SysFile.iCountNumberOfChangedFiles) * "file(s).\n\nRun Check to verify they still compile, and see what is left?") "Back to Check?" to iRetval
                If (iRetval = MBR_Yes) Begin
                    Broadcast Send StartGuidedCheckFromRun of (Client_Id(phoMainPanel(ghoApplication)))
                    Procedure_Return
                End
            End
            // Nothing changed, or the user declined the Check - either way, back to the trail.
            Broadcast Send ActivateGuidedTrail of (Client_Id(phoMainPanel(ghoApplication)))
            Procedure_Return
        End
        /* NOT FOR A SINGLE-FILE RUN (Nils 2026-09-17). Single-file mode exists for a file that has no
           program to compile under - a legacy file dropped beside the workspace, opened on its own from
           the Manual board - so "verify with a compile" is an offer the user cannot take up, and the
           question read as noise right after the run. The editor already shows the rewritten file, which
           is the verification that mode has. A workspace run keeps the offer. */
        Get pbWorkspaceMode of ghoApplication to bWsMode
        If (SysFile.iCountNumberOfChangedFiles > 0 and SysFile.bReadOnly = False and bWsMode = True) Begin
            Get FTYesNoBox ("The run changed" * String(SysFile.iCountNumberOfChangedFiles) * "file(s).\n\nOpen Test Compile to verify the changes still compile cleanly?") "Verify with a compile?" to iRetval
            If (iRetval = MBR_Yes) Begin
                // Mirror the dashboard's Compile-step entry (CI_DashTestCompile): a standing Deep
                // Scan view would keep the bar's Compile chip LOCKED - reset it first so the dock
                // opens ready to compile instead of steering back at the stale scan.
                If (ghoModAnalyzerDock <> 0) ;
                    Send ClearScanView of (oModAnalyzer_grd(ghoModAnalyzerDock))
                Send ShowTestCompilePanel of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))
                Get phoTestCompileFT of ghoApplication to hoTC
                If (hoTC <> 0) Begin
                    Send ShowAnalyzeSummary of hoTC False
                    Send SyncWebButtonStates of hoTC
                End
            End
        End
    End_Procedure

    Procedure ActivateProcess
        Send StartRefactoreCode
    End_Procedure
    
    Procedure ActivateSave
        Send Execute of (oSave_ToolItem(ghoCommandBars))
    End_Procedure

    Procedure ActivateClearAll
        Send Execute of (oClear_MenuItem(ghoCommandBars))
    End_Procedure

    // Build the "Dashboard left / other views right" tab-group layout on demand, instead of relying on
    // CodeJock's fiddly drag-to-split (which also degrades after the tool-panel dock/close churn). Re-asserts
    // ComEnableGroups first (a docked CommandBars dialog-bar may have dropped it), then moves the three work
    // views into ONE new side-by-side group, leaving the Dashboard in the original (left) group. Called by the
    // Main toolbar "Split View" button; ghoTabWorkspace is captured in oCJCommandBarSystem.OnCreateTabbedWorkspace.

    // Helper for SplitViewWorkspace: read the just-activated tab (ComSelected) and move it to iGroup.
    // PumpMsgQueue first so the activation's tab-selection has settled before we read it.
    Procedure _MoveActiveTabToGroup Handle hoTab Integer iGroup
        Variant vItem
        Send PumpMsgQueue of Desktop
        Get ComSelected of hoTab to vItem
        Send ComMoveToGroup of hoTab vItem iGroup
    End_Procedure

    // Helper for SplitViewWorkspace: a SNAPSHOT of every tab in the workspace, taken before anything moves.
    // ComMoveToGroup reorders the workspace's own item list, so a loop that reads ComItem(i) while it moves
    // walks past items (the "loses one view" index shift); collecting first and moving afterwards cannot.
    Function _WorkspaceTabItems Handle hoTab Returns Variant[]
        Variant[] avItems
        Variant   vItem
        Integer   iCount i

        Get ComItemCount of hoTab to iCount
        Move 0 to i
        While (i < iCount)
            Get ComItem of hoTab i to vItem
            Move vItem to avItems[i]
            Increment i
        Loop
        Function_Return avItems
    End_Function

    // TOGGLE the workspace split. ComGroupCount gives the real state - 1 = not split (so split it), >1 =
    // already split (so merge back) - which stops repeated clicks from spawning ever-smaller groups.
    // No window handle / object id needed (a cRDCDbView answers neither, ComFindItem is pure CodeJock):
    // each view is identified by ACTIVATING it and reading the now-selected tab via ComSelected.
    //
    // MERGING SWEEPS EVERY TAB, and does not re-use the split's list of views. What collapses a split is a
    // group going EMPTY, so un-splitting by moving back exactly the three views the split had moved left any
    // other tab holding its group open - and one stray tab is the whole difference between "the split is
    // gone" and "the second click did nothing". A tab the split never touched gets there in several ordinary
    // ways: the Start Center and the Manual Dashboard are views too (both added after this toggle was
    // written), a view opened while the right-hand group is active is CREATED in it, and the closing
    // Activate_oDashboard_vw below opens the Dashboard itself into the active group whenever its tab is not
    // already up. Reading the workspace's own tab list settles all of them at once, and a view added later
    // needs no change here.
    //
    // SPLITTING STAYS NAMED, and that is a DECISION, not the other half of the same bug (Nils, 2026-09-15,
    // asked directly): the three WORK views move right and every other view stays left with the Dashboard -
    // the Start Center and the Manual Dashboard are boards, and a board belongs beside the Dashboard, not
    // stacked with the grids being worked on. So the two halves are deliberately NOT mirrors. Sweeping the
    // tab list is right for the merge, where the goal is only "end up with one group"; it would be wrong
    // here, where WHICH side a view lands on is the whole point. Do not "finish the symmetry".
    Procedure SplitViewWorkspace
        Handle    hoTab
        Variant   vTab vItem vAnchor
        Variant[] avItems
        Integer   iGroup iGroupCount iThis iCount i

        If (ghoCommandBars = 0) Procedure_Return

        // Acquire the live tab workspace on demand (Nils's proven pattern: a fresh DF wrapper bound to the
        // workspace COM object).
        Get Create (RefClass(cCJTabWorkspace)) to hoTab
        Get ComShowTabWorkspace of ghoCommandBars True to vTab
        Set pvComObject of hoTab to vTab

        Get ComGroupCount of hoTab to iGroupCount
        If (iGroupCount > 1) Begin
            // ---- Toggle OFF: gather EVERY tab into the Dashboard's group; the groups that empty
            // auto-collapse, so ComGroupCount returns to 1. ----
            Send Activate_oDashboard_vw of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))
            Send PumpMsgQueue of Desktop
            Get ComSelected of hoTab to vAnchor

            // Snapshot AFTER that activation - it may have opened the Dashboard's tab.
            Get _WorkspaceTabItems hoTab to avItems
            Move (SizeOfArray(avItems)) to iCount

            // The Dashboard's tab is the anchor everything gathers onto. If it cannot be resolved, the
            // FIRST tab does instead: which group wins matters far less than ending up with one, and an
            // unresolvable anchor would otherwise skip every move and leave the split standing silently.
            Get ComFindGroup of hoTab vAnchor to iGroup
            If (iGroup < 0 and iCount > 0) ;
                Move avItems[0] to vAnchor

            Move 0 to i
            While (i < iCount)
                // Re-read the anchor's group every time: a group that collapses renumbers the ones after it.
                Get ComFindGroup of hoTab vAnchor    to iGroup
                Get ComFindGroup of hoTab avItems[i] to iThis
                If (iGroup >= 0 and iThis >= 0 and iThis <> iGroup) ;
                    Send ComMoveToGroup of hoTab avItems[i] iGroup
                Increment i
            Loop
        End
        Else Begin
            // ---- Toggle ON: Dashboard left, the other three in a new VERTICAL (left/right) group.
            // NEWVERTICAL acts on the ACTIVE tab, so activate Folders first; ComFindGroup gives its index. ----
            Send ComEnableGroups of hoTab
            Send Activate_oSelectFoldersView of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))
            Send PumpMsgQueue of Desktop
            Send ComDoWorkspaceCommand of hoTab XTP_ID_WORKSPACE_NEWVERTICAL
            Get ComSelected of hoTab to vItem
            Get ComFindGroup of hoTab vItem to iGroup

            Send Activate_oSelectFunctionsView of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))
            Send _MoveActiveTabToGroup hoTab iGroup
            Send Activate_oEditorView_vw       of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))
            Send _MoveActiveTabToGroup hoTab iGroup
        End

        Send ComRefresh of hoTab
        // Report the state the workspace is REALLY in, not the branch that was taken: a merge that could
        // not collapse the split must not leave the button claiming it did.
        Get ComGroupCount of hoTab to iGroupCount
        Set pbChecked of (oSplitView_MenuItem(ghoCommandBars)) to (iGroupCount > 1)
        Send Destroy of hoTab
        // Dashboard stays in the (left) group; re-select it so it is the focused tab there.
        Send Activate_oDashboard_vw of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars))
    End_Procedure

    Procedure ActivateSourceExplorer
        Send Execute of (oCodeExplorer_ToolbarButton(ghoCommandBars))
    End_Procedure

    // The two settings dialogs, which the Tools menu opens the same way (their toolbar is gone, 2026-11-19).
    Procedure ActivateSettings
        Send Popup of (oProgramSetup_dg(Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)))
    End_Procedure

    Procedure ActivateEditorSettings
        Send Popup of (oScintillaParameters_dg(Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)))
    End_Procedure

    Procedure ActivateUndoRefactoringDialog
        tRFSearchResult[] BackpupFileArray
        Get AllBackupFolderFiles of ghoApplication to BackpupFileArray
        Send FillBackupFilesDialog of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)) BackpupFileArray
    End_Procedure

    /* Migration step 0 - what to copy to the new location. A DEVELOPMENT entry point for now: the
       dialog is the first piece of the Prepare flow, and the flow that will call it for real (copy,
       then write the target-version .sws, then retarget the libraries) does not exist yet. When it
       does, this becomes a step in that sequence and the shortcut can go. */
    Procedure ActivateCopyScopeDialog
        tCopyItem[] aChosen
        String sDest sVer
        Boolean bOk
        Get SelectMigrationCopyScope of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)) to aChosen
        If (SizeOfArray(aChosen) = 0) ;
            Procedure_Return          // cancelled, or nothing ticked - same action either way
        Get MigrationCopyDestination of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)) to sDest
        Get psTargetDfVersion of ghoApplication to sVer
        Get RunWorkspaceCopy of (Client_Id(ghoCommandBars)) aChosen sDest sVer to bOk
    End_Procedure

    /* Library Maintenance on the workspace that is OPEN - the in-place counterpart to the copy
       flow's call, which points the same dialog at the copy it has just written. "" means "the
       loaded workspace", which MaintainWorkspaceLibraries resolves itself. */
    Procedure ActivateLibraryMaintenance
        Boolean bOk
        Get MaintainWorkspaceLibraries "" to bOk
    End_Procedure

    Procedure Switch_Prior_View
        Send Switch_Prior_View of (ClientAreaObject (ghoCommandBars))
    End_Procedure

    Procedure Switch_Next_View
        Send Switch_Next_View of (ClientAreaObject (ghoCommandBars))
    End_Procedure

    Procedure ToggleActionButton
        Integer iActiveView
        Handle  hoView
        Get piActiveView of ghoApplication to iActiveView
        If (iActiveView = CI_CleanupSource) Begin
            Get phoActiveView of ghoApplication to hoView
            Send ToggleActionButton of hoView
        End
    End_Procedure
    
//    Cant't have this as it collides with the DD_Debug dialog...
//    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_D  Send ActivateEditorSettings
    /* Alt+E, Alt+F, Alt+T and Alt+W open the Edit, File, Tools and Workspace menus (2026-11-19): Alt plus a letter
       is how a menu bar opens. Their commands keep their Ctrl keys - Source Explorer, the workspace/file switch,
       Settings and Open Workspace. */
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_D   Send ActivateEditorSettings
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_E  Send ActivateSourceExplorer
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_F  Send ActivateFileRadioButton
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_G   Send ToggleActionButton
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_G  Send ToggleActionButton
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_L   Send ShowLogFile of ghoApplication
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_M   Send ActivateCompare   // Ctrl+M freed for the editor view's Modernize-dock toggle (EditorViewFT.vw)
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_O  Send ActivateBrowseDialog
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_O   Send ActivateBrowseDialog
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_P   Send ActivateCopyScopeDialog   // Prepare migration - what to copy (dev entry point)
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_B   Send ActivateLibraryMaintenance  // Library maintenance for the open workspace
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_F5 Send ActivateProcess
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_S  Send ActivateSave
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_S   Send ActivateSave
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_T  Send ActivateSettings
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_U   Send ActivateUndoRefactoringDialog
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_W  Send ActivateWorkspaceDialog
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_X   Send Exit_Application
    On_Key Key_F2          Send ActivateSave
//    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_F4 Send ActivateBrowseDialog

    // On_Key constant for Ctrl+Shift+Tab: C_CtrlShiftTab, RefactorConstants.h.pkg

    Procedure End_Construct_Object
        Forward Send End_Construct_Object
        Set Icon to "DFRefactor.ico"
    End_Procedure

    On_Key C_CtrlShiftTab   Send Switch_Prior_View
    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_Tab Send Switch_Next_View
End_Object

Use cCIScan.pkg

/* THE CI SCAN, run from OnStartup when the command line said /scan <ini> (2026-11-20 - cCIScan.pkg says why it
   works the way it does). Analyze Source over the INI's folders, or the workspace's source folders when it names
   none. It changes nothing: the findings go to the JSON and the SARIF file, each marked new or unchanged against
   the baseline - or, with /baseline, become the baseline. Then the program ENDS, with exit code 0 (no new
   findings), 1 (new findings) or 2 (the scan could not run), and the result file the INI names says the same. */
Procedure RunCIScanAndExit
    Handle hoScan
    tCompileError[] aMsgs
    tCIScanFinding[] aFindings
    tCIScanReport Report
    tCIScanBaseline Baseline
    tSarifLog Sarif
    String[] asFolders asBaseline
    String sError sHome sSws sNow sSummary sBaselineFile sWhy sFilter sCRLF sJsonFile sSarifFile sBaseCreated
    Integer i iLast iScanExit iFilesTotal iCacheHits iNew iGone iShown iRet
    Boolean bCancelled bFound bOK bBaseline

    Move (Character(13) + Character(10)) to sCRLF
    Get Create (RefClass(cCIScan)) to hoScan
    Move 0 to iNew
    Move 0 to iGone
    Move 0 to iFilesTotal
    Move False to bFound
    Get psScanError of ghoApplication to sError
    If (sError = "") Begin
        Get psSWSFile    of ghoApplication to sSws
        Get psHomeTarget of ghoApplication to sHome
        If (sSws = "" or Trim(sHome) = "") ;
            Move ("the workspace could not be opened: " + sSws) to sError
    End
    If (sError = "") Begin
        Get pasScanFolders of ghoApplication to asFolders
        If (SizeOfArray(asFolders) = 0) ;
            Get WorkspaceSourceRoots of ghoApplication to asFolders
        Move (SizeOfArray(asFolders) - 1) to iLast
        If (iLast < 0) ;
            Move "there are no source folders to scan" to sError
        // A folder that is not there fails the run: scanning less than the INI asks for, and passing, is the worst outcome.
        // So does a FILE named as a folder - vPathIsDirectory, since vFolderExists is True for an existing file (2026-11-20).
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (sError = "") Begin
                If (vPathIsDirectory(asFolders[i]) = False) Begin
                    If (vFilePathExists(asFolders[i]) = True) ;
                        Move ("the INI names a file, not a folder: " + asFolders[i]) to sError
                    Else ;
                        Move ("a folder the INI names is not there: " + asFolders[i]) to sError
                End
            End
        Loop
    End
    If (sError = "") Begin
        // The INI's file filter, in the buffer for this run - never saved, so the stored filter stays the user's.
        Get psScanFilter of ghoApplication to sFilter
        If (sFilter <> "") ;
            Move sFilter to SysFile.FileExtensionFilter
        Get ScanFoldersToMessages of ghoDeepScanDriver asFolders "CI scan - Analyze Source..." (&bCancelled) (&iFilesTotal) (&iCacheHits) to aMsgs
        If (bCancelled = True) ;
            Move "the scan was cancelled" to sError
        Else If (iFilesTotal = 0) ;
            Move "no source files were found in the folders to scan" to sError
    End
    If (sError = "") Begin
        Get FindingsFromMessages of hoScan (&aMsgs) sHome to aFindings
        Get TodayIsoDateTime of ghoApplication to sNow
        Get pbScanBaseline     of ghoApplication to bBaseline
        Get psScanBaselineFile of ghoApplication to sBaselineFile
        If (bBaseline = True) Begin
            Get BaselineFor of hoScan (&aFindings) sSws sNow to Baseline
            Get WriteBaseline of hoScan Baseline sBaselineFile to bOK
            If (bOK = False) ;
                Move ("the baseline file could not be written: " + sBaselineFile) to sError
            Else Begin
                Move True to bFound
                Move CI_CIScanPass to iScanExit
                Move (String(SizeOfArray(aFindings)) + " finding(s) in " + String(iFilesTotal) + " file(s) are the baseline now:" + sCRLF + sBaselineFile) to sSummary
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get BaselineFingerprints of hoScan sBaselineFile (&bFound) (&sBaseCreated) (&sWhy) to asBaseline
            If (sWhy <> "") ;
                Move sWhy to sError
            Else Begin
                Get MarkNewFindings of hoScan (&aFindings) asBaseline (&iGone) to iNew
                Move (If(iNew > 0, CI_CIScanNewFindings, CI_CIScanPass)) to iScanExit
                Move (String(SizeOfArray(aFindings)) + " finding(s) in " + String(iFilesTotal) + " file(s): " + String(iNew) + " new, " + String(SizeOfArray(aFindings) - iNew) + " in the baseline.") to sSummary
                If (iGone > 0) ;
                    Move (sSummary + " " + String(iGone) + " of the baseline's are gone.") to sSummary
                // The baseline it was compared with, by name, size and date: which file decides is never a guess.
                If (bFound = False) ;
                    Move (sSummary + sCRLF + "There is no baseline file, so every finding counts as new. Run once with /baseline to accept today's findings:" + sCRLF + sBaselineFile) to sSummary
                Else ;
                    Move (sSummary + sCRLF + "Baseline: " + sBaselineFile + " - " + String(SizeOfArray(asBaseline)) + " finding(s), written " + sBaseCreated + ".") to sSummary
                // The first new ones, for the build log; the SARIF and the JSON file have them all.
                Move 0 to iShown
                Move (SizeOfArray(aFindings) - 1) to iLast
                For i from 0 to iLast
                    If (aFindings[i].bNew = True) Begin
                        Increment iShown
                        If (iShown <= 25) ;
                            Move (sSummary + sCRLF + "  NEW " + aFindings[i].sRule + " " + aFindings[i].sFile + ":" + String(aFindings[i].iLine) + "  " + aFindings[i].sSymbol) to sSummary
                    End
                Loop
                If (iShown > 25) ;
                    Move (sSummary + sCRLF + "  ... and " + String(iShown - 25) + " more") to sSummary
            End
        End
    End
    If (sError = "") Begin
        Move CI_CIScanVersion  to Report.iVersion
        Move sSws              to Report.sWorkspace
        Move sNow              to Report.sCreated
        Move sBaselineFile     to Report.sBaselineFile
        Move bFound            to Report.bBaselineFound
        Move iFilesTotal       to Report.iFilesScanned
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFindings)) to Report.iFindings
        Move iNew              to Report.iNew
        Move iGone             to Report.iGone
        Move iScanExit         to Report.iExitCode
        Move aFindings         to Report.aFindings
        Get psScanJsonFile  of ghoApplication to sJsonFile
        Get psScanSarifFile of ghoApplication to sSarifFile
        Get WriteReport of hoScan Report sJsonFile to bOK
        If (bOK = False) ;
            Move ("the JSON file could not be written: " + sJsonFile) to sError
        Else Begin
            Get SarifFor of hoScan (&aFindings) sHome to Sarif
            Get WriteSarif of hoScan Sarif sSarifFile to bOK
            If (bOK = False) ;
                Move ("the SARIF file could not be written: " + sSarifFile) to sError
            Else ;
                Move (sSummary + sCRLF + "JSON: " + sJsonFile + sCRLF + "SARIF: " + sSarifFile) to sSummary
        End
    End
    If (sError <> "") Begin
        Move CI_CIScanError to iScanExit
        Move ("The CI scan could not run: " + sError + ".") to sSummary
    End
    Send WriteResultFile of hoScan (psBatchResultFile(ghoApplication)) iScanExit (TodayIsoDateTime(ghoApplication)) sSummary
    Send Destroy of hoScan
    // /bm's way out: TerminateProcess carries the exit code (ExitProcess deadlocks on COM detach).
    Move (TerminateProcessEf(-1, iScanExit)) to iRet
    Send Exit_Application
End_Procedure

Procedure OnStartup
    Handle hoBatchDD hoBatchFolderDD

    // This is weird. If this program is started from the TestBench,
    // the icon in Windows task bar is not showing. And the following line doesn't help either.
    Set Icon of (phoMainPanel(ghoApplication)) to "DFRefactor.ico"

    // The status panel in the FT colours - FTColorPanel (RDCFlexTron). Here rather than beside the object,
    // because the object lives in a SHARED package the two light builds also compile. By this point every
    // object exists and the theme has been read, which is what the colouring needs.
    Send FTColorPanel ghoStatusPanel

    /* THE CI SCAN (/scan <ini>, 2026-11-20) comes first, and ends the program. pbBatchMode is set for it too,
       to keep every dialog away, so the refactoring batch below must never follow it. */
    If (pbScanMode(ghoApplication) = True) Begin
        Send RunCIScanAndExit
        Procedure_Return
    End
    
    If (pbBatchMode(ghoApplication) = True) Begin
        Set pbBatchMode of ghoEngine to True
        // The INI's per-function parameters go into the table before the run (the engine
        // reads them from FunctionsA.Parameter) and the user's own values go back after -
        // a batch run must leave the standing configuration as it found it.
        Get Create (RefClass(cFunctionsDataDictionary)) to hoBatchDD
        Send ApplyCmdLineFunctionParameters of ghoApplication hoBatchDD
        // ...and the INI's function ticks and file filter, the user's own saved first (2026-11-20).
        Send ApplyCmdLineSelections of ghoApplication hoBatchDD
        // The command line's folders ticked for the run, so the Start Center's Source folders line shows what
        // the run works on; ExitBatchWithCode puts the earlier ticks back (Nils 2026-10-24).
        Get Create (RefClass(cFolderSelHeaDataDictionary)) to hoBatchFolderDD
        Send ApplyCmdLineFolderTicks of ghoApplication hoBatchFolderDD
        Broadcast Send RequestTileRefresh of (Client_Id(phoMainPanel(ghoApplication)))
        Send StartRefactoreCode of (phoMainPanel(ghoApplication))
        Send RestoreCmdLineFunctionParameters of ghoApplication
        Send RestoreCmdLineFolderTicks of ghoApplication
        Send RestoreCmdLineSelections of ghoApplication
        Send Destroy of hoBatchFolderDD
        Send Destroy of hoBatchDD
        // A batch run that gets back here never reached ExitBatchWithCode: it stopped before the engine ran
        // (a blank file filter, for one). Exit with STATUS=FAILED rather than go on to Start_UI and wait with
        // the window open (live run, 2026-10-24).
        Send ExitBatchWithCode of ghoApplication eEngineError "The run stopped before any file was refactored: check the CmdLine INI's folders, file filter and functions."
    End
End_Procedure
Send OnStartup

//  - If you get compile error: "Can't include resource ..\HELP\ABOUTFT.HTML",
//    the About text, Help\AboutFT.html, is missing: AboutFT.pkg compiles it in as a resource
//    (since 2026-10-06; it was AboutFT.rtf in a RichEdit before). It can be empty, but it must exist.
//
// -  If you get compile Error 4295: "xxx Can't include resource FILELISTBACKUPFILE.CFG",
//    you will need to manually make a copy of the Filelist.cfg in the Data folder -> "FilelistBackupFile.cfg"
Start_UI
